WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.302
-For those who are missing out,
you play an ex-FBI agent...

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:04.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Current CIA agent, Black Ops.

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:08.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ex-FBI agent, ex-CIA agent,
current Black Ops.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:10.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
So maybe FBI --
-So you can't keep a job.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
You play a person who just
cannot hold down a job.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, she's
a person of interest.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:17.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
She can't hold a job at all.
-You have --

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.552 size:81% position:41%
-I'm constantly fired.
I'm constantly framed.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I can't believe
you keep getting rehired.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:24.157
I feel like Black Ops should
have looked at your resumé

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.658 line:92%
and said, "I got to be honest.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
FBI and CIA
both kicked you out."

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:28.862 size:81% position:41%
-Well, I don't know if
they kicked her out.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
Last time she --
the end of season two,

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:32.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
she gave up everything.
-Okay, got you.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She was like,
"I always get framed because

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm the brown girl."
-Okay.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
-FBI does not like me.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm out. Peace.
-Okay.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, but in season three --
-You know what?

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:44.477
I want a simple job where I just
fight people on fire escapes.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:45.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which is what she does.
-Yeah.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.815
-She moves to Italy and she
settles in beautiful Tuscany,

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Montepulciano
for three years.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:53.420
And we pick up this season three
years later, which is amazing

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause if you haven't seen the
first two seasons,

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.257
it doesn't matter.
You can just start season three.

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:59.292
-And the other thing that's
amazing is you actually got

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go to Tuscany.
Were you so happy when you saw

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:02.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
that in the scripts?
-I did.

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:04.664
I was so excited, but I also
felt terrible because I was

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.699
the only cast member that went.
-Oh, right.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.635
'Cause everybody else had
to stay in the fake CIA.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:12.372
Yeah, everybody has to be
in fake Italy in New York.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But I got to go because

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.709
I had to be really beautiful
in the vineyards and everything,

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was amazing.
And I felt super bad.

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:22.449
So I brought everyone wine from
Montepulciano, where we were.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's very nice.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.651
'Cause I was like,
you know, you can experience --

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.586
-Did you really, or did you get
home and go to a wine store

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.422 size:78% position:39%
and say, "I need wine
from Montepulciano"?

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.824 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-It says Montepulciano.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:31.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I could have done
that in New York.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
-But no, I didn't.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. That's very nice.
-I got it with me.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:38.131
May have got it with me
for myself, and then felt guilty

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I arrived in New York.
-And so you caved.

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were like, "I got a bottle
for you guys to share."

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and just -- no.
-Yeah.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here's some Dixie cups,
and do it up.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:47.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no.
-Now, obviously, there's a lot

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
of physical work on the show.
A lot of fighting.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.111 line:92%
How was your fighting skills?

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I always do
my own stunts.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:53.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
That's impressive.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.483
-And now, I think -- this weird
thing has started happening

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
to me, you guys.
I think I've been doing --

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
being Alex Parrish
for three seasons now,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.190
I've started to believe that
I have her fighting skills.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.325 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Oh, yeah, that's bad.

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.126 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:07.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I mean, if I get mugged

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
in New York, I'm going to be,
like, all ready for it.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And then someone's

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
just going to slap me,
and I'll be out.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.935
-Well say, that was actually --
I hate to say this,

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
as they're taking your purse,
they'll be like,

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
"That was easier
than most muggings."

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We should -- You should
not have tried that.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.542
-Like, as soon as you did that,
I was like, "This is going

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be super easy."
-I'll be like -- wah!

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:27.347
Or something.
-You also got to go to Ireland.

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:30.483
-Yes, we shot in Ireland.
Dublin, which was amazing.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And your mom came.
That's a picture of you

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
and your mom,
in a pub it looks like.

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:34.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think my mom
just came for the beer.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.724 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah. She's a beer fan?
-Yeah. She's a beer fan.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:38.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
But also --
-You guys gotta learn,

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can get all these alcohols
wherever you were.

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.996
You don't have to travel.
-Yeah, but it's Ireland.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is.
-And I think my mom just makes

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
excuses to come and visit me
when I'm in, like,

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:48.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
really interesting places
in the world.

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:52.739
So she just, like, uses me
to actually visit this place.

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:54.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, but I mean,
you still benefit.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
You get to hang out
with your mom.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
And she's super cool.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.378
-And it seems like you've chosen
to hang out with your mom a lot,

00:02:58.378 --> 00:02:59.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she is
your producing partner.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:03.783
-Yeah, we're business partners.
That's a lot of fun.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:04.684 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:05.952 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.987
How long --
-You can never yell at your mom.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Like, you know, when

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:11.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's a problem, or if
you're having a disagreement,

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:13.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
she always just
gives you the eyes.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:15.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, she always
just gives me the eye.

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:17.931 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:20.066
It's, like, disappointed.
And then I'm just like,

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Fine, we'll do
whatever you want."

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:24.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So obviously, you bring
a lot of creativity

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:25.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
to this producer-ing
partnership.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.806 size:81% position:41%
-Yes, that's the deal.
-What does she bring?

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am the creative,
she's business.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
-I don't understand money

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:32.579 size:88% position:44%
and, like, taxes and all
that complicated stuff.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:34.914
So she does all of that, whereas
I do all the creative stuff.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And was that your whole life?
Was she the one that was

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.918
locked in on money and business?
-You know, it was amazing.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:41.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, my dad didn't know
anything about money.

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:44.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
So -- and my mom was always
financially, like, very acute.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:47.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
So one day he was just like,
"I don't understand this.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here's my wallet.
This is what we make."

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:51.931
And now my mom started
putting credit cards and,

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.533 line:92%
like, cash in his wallet.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I still
get pocket money.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She's a put-pocket?
-I think so.

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.639 line:92%
Yeah, she's a put-pocket.

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:00.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God, $100.
-I need to use that.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How did this happen?
-It's like, "Where did I get

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
this money from?
I'm rich."

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:07.313
-You, as a producer, you produce
films all over the world.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:10.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you've done
50 movies in India.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Give or take.
-In Bollywood.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In India.
In Bollywood.

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:14.520 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-In Bollywood. So --

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.688 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:18.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I want to ask about this,
because obviously I --

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:21.928
and I'm guilty of this as well,
I believe Bollywood to be

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:23.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
a genre of films,
but that's not the case.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, and that's
what annoys me so much.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:28.334
I mean, I don't even think
I realized that when I was

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:31.738
in India working in Hindi films
that Bollywood has been reduced

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:36.209
to a genre, when it's not.
It's actually an entire industry

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:38.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
of movies which
is action, drama.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:40.947 size:78% position:39%
It's like Hollywood.
But we're not even --

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:42.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bollywood's not even a place.
-Yeah.

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hollywood's a real place.
-Right.

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:48.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
-At Trader Joe's, I saw
Bollywood-flavored popcorn.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:49.122 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:52.792 size:84% position:42%
How do you put a flavor
to an entire industry?

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-What would Hollywood's

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
flavor be?
Like cheeseburger?

00:04:56.663 --> 00:04:59.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
No, it would be gluten free.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.167 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Gluten free.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
Soy latte.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With no soy.
-Exactly.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
It would be latte popcorn.
-Yeah.

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:09.976
-So it's like, what is annoying
is that it gets reduced to such

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:11.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
a stereotype,
which it's really not.

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:14.714
Not every Bollywood movie,
though music is a very important

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:17.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
part of our movies,
but they're not all,

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.686 size:81% position:41%
break out into random,
synchronized dancing.

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:22.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every industry has
it's own stereotype.

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:24.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every country has
it's own stereotype.

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:27.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you work with, obviously,
the Indian film industry

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.695
so much.
What is the stereotype they have

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:31.597 size:81% position:41%
about American films?
-Well, I think like --

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:34.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
aliens only land in America.
-Yeah, that's true.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:35.501 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.203 line:92%
That's a really good point.

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.805 line:92%
-I want an alien in India.

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:41.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. You know --
-I want E.T.

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:42.575 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Well, that's the thing.

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:45.611
You can't say you want an alien,
'cause very rarely are they E.T.

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:48.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, one out of every
100 times, there is somebody

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
who just wants
to get out of there.

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:50.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, they're usually trying
to eat your brains.

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:53.686
But I'd like to see what, like,
other parts of the world would

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:54.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
do when that happens.
-Right.

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:56.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know?
-I'm just worried that you

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:58.825
will panic, and then you
will break out into song.

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:00.193 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Hey, I'm Alex Parrish.

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:02.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll break out into a song,
and kick butt.

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:03.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, well then...
-How about that?

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:04.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...I will buy
a ticket for that.

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:06.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

